---
description: UI work in the Next.js web app. Routes to the design-engineering skills and the design contract.
globs: web/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Before touching UI in `web/`:

1. Read `web/DESIGN.md`. It is the contract: tokens, the two easing curves, the z-index scale, the motion budget and the explicit exceptions. Do not introduce a colour, font, radius, shadow, easing or z-index that is not declared there; propose an addition to `DESIGN.md` instead.
2. Apply the `baseline-ui` skill (`.agents/skills/baseline-ui/SKILL.md`) to every edit: accessible primitives from `@base-ui/react` (never hand-rolled focus or keyboard behaviour), `aria-label` on icon buttons, `AlertDialog` for destructive actions, `text-balance` on headings and `text-pretty` on body, `tabular-nums` on data, `h-dvh` not `h-screen`, safe-area insets on fixed elements, errors next to the action, one accent per view, no gradients.
3. Before adding or changing any animation, run it through `emil-design-eng` (`.agents/skills/emil-design-eng/SKILL.md`): frequency → purpose → easing → duration. Keyboard-initiated and 100+/day interactions do not animate. Interaction feedback ≤ 200 ms, enter/exit ≤ 300 ms, `transform`/`opacity` only, `ease-out` on entrance, never `ease-in`, never from `scale(0)`. Landing-page reveals are the only surface allowed past 300 ms.
4. Before adding a UI dependency, consult `pick-ui-library` (`.agents/skills/pick-ui-library/SKILL.md`). Current picks in use: `@base-ui/react`, `sonner`, `input-otp`, `@number-flow/react`, `motion`, `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` via `cn()`.
5. For a review or cleanup request, use `review-animations` for motion and `improve-ui` (read-only, writes to `design-plans/`) for everything else. Do not implement audit findings without the user selecting them.

Verification for any UI change: `pnpm -C web lint`, `npx -C web tsc --noEmit`, and the relevant `agent/scripts/e2e_*.py` flow when selectors or flows changed.
